= Rutherford B. Hayes

Rutherford B. Hayes of Ohio is a war hero whose combat record speaks for itself: Wounded five times and promoted to brevet major general for valor. Unlike many <span style="color: #c00000;">**Republican**</span> politicians, Hayes carries the credibility of genuine sacrifice. His reputation for integrity and honesty is uncommon in an era of machine politics and corruption scandals.

Hayes represents the **<span style="color: #9D2933;">Moderate Republican</span>** who believes in Reconstruction without radicalism, and in honest government without self-dealing. As Chairman of the Joint Committee on the Library of Congress, he controls significant cultural patronage. His standing with the Army officer corps remains strong from his wartime service.

